// M2's exit (docs/ROADMAP.md, exit criteria; review 7fnfdhb5): the
// owner's live use played through headless, as a person would, by
// commands, keys and typing. A document with pictures, in Book, and a
// Markdown file with headings, emphasis, a list, a task list, a quote,
// code, a link and a table are written; xWorks quits; it starts again, in
// a new document as without a file, and both are opened, each as it was
// left, the Markdown byte for byte where it isn't edited after; and both
// are printed to PDF, by Export as PDF, which writes beside each the PDF
// that Print hands the system. shot draws both documents' pages
// (`exit-m2-pages`), and crates/app/tests/sessions.rs checks that each
// reopens as it was left and prints the same pages, its text extractable.
(
    size: (1100, 760),
    language: Some("en-GB"),
    copy: [
        ("crates/app/tests/pictures/gradient.jpg", "Pictures/gradient.jpg"),
        ("crates/app/tests/pictures/turned.jpg", "Pictures/turned.jpg"),
    ],
    events: [
        // The document with pictures, in a new document, given Book.
        CommandWith("replace-stylesheet", [Text("app:Book")]),
        Key("Primary+1"),
        Type("The garden in spring"),
        Key("Enter"),
        Type("Every spring the garden wakes in the same order. The snowdrops come first, under the hedge, then the crocuses along the path, and by the time the daffodils open the beds are ready to be dug. This year the soil was dry enough by the middle of March, and the first rows went in a fortnight early."),
        Key("Enter"),
        Type("The beds were dug over and raked to a fine tilth "),
        Command("insert-picture"),
        Choose(Some("Pictures/gradient.jpg")),
        Type(" and the paths between them edged with boards, so that nobody treads on the soil once it is sown. A strip of fleece kept the frost off the earliest rows."),
        Key("Enter"),
        Key("Primary+2"),
        Type("What was sown"),
        Key("Enter"),
        Command("list-numbers"),
        Type("Broad beans, Aquadulce, in a double row"),
        Key("Enter"),
        Type("Peas, Kelvedon Wonder, against the netting"),
        Key("Enter"),
        Type("Lettuce, Little Gem, a short row every fortnight"),
        Key("Enter"),
        Key("Enter"),
        Type("Each row was labelled with its date, and the labels photographed for the record "),
        Command("insert-picture"),
        Choose(Some("Pictures/turned.jpg")),
        Type(", which keeps the sowings straight from one year to the next."),
        Key("Enter"),
        Key("Primary+2"),
        Type("What it cost"),
        Key("Enter"),
        Type("Seeds\t12.40"),
        Key("Enter"),
        Type("Fleece and netting\t8.95"),
        Key("Enter"),
        Type("Boards for the paths\t21.50"),
        // The costs without Body's indent, their figures on their decimal
        // points near the column's end, dots leading to them, from the
        // Text tab.
        Key("Shift+Up"),
        Key("Shift+Up"),
        Key("Shift+Home"),
        CommandWith("paragraph-style", [Text("First Paragraph")]),
        CommandWith("tab-stop-add", [Int(3744000), Text("decimal:.")]),
        CommandWith("tab-stop-leader", [Int(3744000), Text(".")]),
        Key("Primary+End"),
        Key("Enter"),
        CommandWith("paragraph-style", [Text("Body")]),
        Type("Next spring the beds move round by one, so nothing grows where it grew the year before."),
        Key("Enter"),
        Key("Primary+2"),
        Type("Next year"),
        Key("Enter"),
        Type("The beans will go where the brassicas were, and the brassicas where the potatoes grew, the ground limed for them in the autumn. The peas will have a taller netting, as this year they climbed past the top of it by June and leaned over the path, and the lettuce will be sown in shorter rows, more often, so that there is never a glut and never a gap."),
        Key("Enter"),
        Type("Whatever is sown, the garden is written up again in the spring, with its pictures, and printed for the shed wall, where last year's sheet has faded but is still legible."),
        Name("The garden in spring"),

        // The Markdown file, in a window of its own.
        Command("new-markdown"),
        Key("Primary+1"),
        Type("Garden notes"),
        Key("Enter"),
        Type("Notes kept as "),
        Key("Primary+I"),
        Type("plain text"),
        Key("Primary+I"),
        Type(", which any editor reads, the "),
        Key("Primary+B"),
        Type("important"),
        Key("Primary+B"),
        Type(" parts in bold. More on growing beans at www.example.org"),
        // A space after an address makes it a link.
        Type(" "),
        Type("whenever it rains."),
        Key("Enter"),
        Key("Primary+2"),
        Type("To sow"),
        Key("Enter"),
        Key("Primary+Shift+8"),
        Type("Beans"),
        Key("Enter"),
        Type("Peas"),
        Key("Enter"),
        Key("Enter"),
        Key("Primary+2"),
        Type("To do"),
        Key("Enter"),
        Command("list-tasks"),
        Type("Dig the bed"),
        Key("Enter"),
        Type("Mend the netting"),
        Key("Up"),
        Command("task-toggle"),
        Key("Primary+End"),
        Key("Enter"),
        Key("Enter"),
        Key("Primary+Shift+9"),
        Type("Sow little and often."),
        Key("Enter"),
        Key("Enter"),
        Type("The rotation, as code:"),
        Key("Enter"),
        Key("Primary+Shift+C"),
        Type("beds = [\"roots\", \"legumes\", \"brassicas\"]"),
        Key("Enter"),
        Type("next = beds[(year + 1) % 3]"),
        Key("Enter"),
        Key("Enter"),
        Type("Yields:"),
        Key("Enter"),
        Key("Primary+Shift+T"),
        Type("Crop"),
        Key("Tab"),
        Type("Rows"),
        Key("Tab"),
        Type("Beans"),
        Key("Tab"),
        Type("2"),
        Key("Tab"),
        Type("Peas"),
        Key("Tab"),
        Type("3"),
        // Down leaves the table, for the paragraph after it.
        Key("Down"),
        Type("More peas next year."),
        Name("Garden notes"),
        Saved("Garden notes.md", "# Garden notes\n\nNotes kept as *plain text*, which any editor reads, the **important** parts in bold. More on growing beans at www.example.org whenever it rains.\n\n## To sow\n\n- Beans\n- Peas\n\n## To do\n\n- [x] Dig the bed\n- [ ] Mend the netting\n\n> Sow little and often.\n\nThe rotation, as code:\n\n```\nbeds = [\"roots\", \"legumes\", \"brassicas\"]\nnext = beds[(year + 1) % 3]\n```\n\nYields:\n\n| Crop  | Rows |\n| ----- | ---- |\n| Beans | 2    |\n| Peas  | 3    |\n\nMore peas next year.\n"),

        // xWorks quits, and starts again; both are opened.
        Command("quit"),
        Command("open"),
        Choose(Some("Garden notes.md")),
        Name("Garden notes"),
        // As it was left, byte for byte, and as it was read.
        Saved("Garden notes.md", "# Garden notes\n\nNotes kept as *plain text*, which any editor reads, the **important** parts in bold. More on growing beans at www.example.org whenever it rains.\n\n## To sow\n\n- Beans\n- Peas\n\n## To do\n\n- [x] Dig the bed\n- [ ] Mend the netting\n\n> Sow little and often.\n\nThe rotation, as code:\n\n```\nbeds = [\"roots\", \"legumes\", \"brassicas\"]\nnext = beds[(year + 1) % 3]\n```\n\nYields:\n\n| Crop  | Rows |\n| ----- | ---- |\n| Beans | 2    |\n| Peas  | 3    |\n\nMore peas next year.\n"),
        Outline([
            "Heading 1: Garden notes",
            "Body: Notes kept as plain text, which any editor reads, the important parts in bold. More on growing beans at www.example.org whenever it rains.",
            "Heading 2: To sow",
            "list",
            "  item",
            "    Body: Beans",
            "  item",
            "    Body: Peas",
            "Heading 2: To do",
            "list",
            "  item task",
            "    Body: Dig the bed",
            "  item",
            "    Body: Mend the netting",
            "quote",
            "  Body: Sow little and often.",
            "Body: The rotation, as code:",
            "Code: beds = [\"roots\", \"legumes\", \"brassicas\"]\u{2028}next = beds[(year + 1) % 3]",
            "Body: Yields:",
            "table",
            "  row",
            "    Table Header: Crop",
            "    Table Header: Rows",
            "  row",
            "    Body: Beans",
            "    Body: 2",
            "  row",
            "    Body: Peas",
            "    Body: 3",
            "Body: More peas next year.",
        ]),
        // An edit after it was opened again changes its line alone.
        Key("Primary+Home"),
        Key("Down"),
        Type("Spring 2026. "),
        Saved("Garden notes.md", "# Garden notes\n\nSpring 2026. Notes kept as *plain text*, which any editor reads, the **important** parts in bold. More on growing beans at www.example.org whenever it rains.\n\n## To sow\n\n- Beans\n- Peas\n\n## To do\n\n- [x] Dig the bed\n- [ ] Mend the netting\n\n> Sow little and often.\n\nThe rotation, as code:\n\n```\nbeds = [\"roots\", \"legumes\", \"brassicas\"]\nnext = beds[(year + 1) % 3]\n```\n\nYields:\n\n| Crop  | Rows |\n| ----- | ---- |\n| Beans | 2    |\n| Peas  | 3    |\n\nMore peas next year.\n"),
        Command("export-pdf"),
        Command("open"),
        Choose(Some("The garden in spring.xw")),
        Name("The garden in spring"),
        Command("export-pdf"),
    ],
    // The document with pictures, as it was left.
    expect: [
        ("Heading 1", "The garden in spring"),
        ("Body", "Every spring the garden wakes in the same order. The snowdrops come first, under the hedge, then the crocuses along the path, and by the time the daffodils open the beds are ready to be dug. This year the soil was dry enough by the middle of March, and the first rows went in a fortnight early."),
        ("Body", "The beds were dug over and raked to a fine tilth \u{fffc} and the paths between them edged with boards, so that nobody treads on the soil once it is sown. A strip of fleece kept the frost off the earliest rows."),
        ("Heading 2", "What was sown"),
        ("Body", "Broad beans, Aquadulce, in a double row"),
        ("Body", "Peas, Kelvedon Wonder, against the netting"),
        ("Body", "Lettuce, Little Gem, a short row every fortnight"),
        ("Body", "Each row was labelled with its date, and the labels photographed for the record \u{fffc}, which keeps the sowings straight from one year to the next."),
        ("Heading 2", "What it cost"),
        ("First Paragraph", "Seeds\t12.40"),
        ("First Paragraph", "Fleece and netting\t8.95"),
        ("First Paragraph", "Boards for the paths\t21.50"),
        ("Body", "Next spring the beds move round by one, so nothing grows where it grew the year before."),
        ("Heading 2", "Next year"),
        ("Body", "The beans will go where the brassicas were, and the brassicas where the potatoes grew, the ground limed for them in the autumn. The peas will have a taller netting, as this year they climbed past the top of it by June and leaned over the path, and the lettuce will be sown in shorter rows, more often, so that there is never a glut and never a gap."),
        ("Body", "Whatever is sown, the garden is written up again in the spring, with its pictures, and printed for the shed wall, where last year's sheet has faded but is still legible."),
    ],
    outline: Some([
        "Heading 1: The garden in spring",
        "Body: Every spring the garden wakes in the same order. The snowdrops come first, under the hedge, then the crocuses along the path, and by the time the daffodils open the beds are ready to be dug. This year the soil was dry enough by the middle of March, and the first rows went in a fortnight early.",
        "Body: The beds were dug over and raked to a fine tilth \u{fffc} and the paths between them edged with boards, so that nobody treads on the soil once it is sown. A strip of fleece kept the frost off the earliest rows.",
        "Heading 2: What was sown",
        "list ordered",
        "  item",
        "    Body: Broad beans, Aquadulce, in a double row",
        "  item",
        "    Body: Peas, Kelvedon Wonder, against the netting",
        "  item",
        "    Body: Lettuce, Little Gem, a short row every fortnight",
        "Body: Each row was labelled with its date, and the labels photographed for the record \u{fffc}, which keeps the sowings straight from one year to the next.",
        "Heading 2: What it cost",
        "First Paragraph: Seeds\t12.40",
        "First Paragraph: Fleece and netting\t8.95",
        "First Paragraph: Boards for the paths\t21.50",
        "Body: Next spring the beds move round by one, so nothing grows where it grew the year before.",
        "Heading 2: Next year",
        "Body: The beans will go where the brassicas were, and the brassicas where the potatoes grew, the ground limed for them in the autumn. The peas will have a taller netting, as this year they climbed past the top of it by June and leaned over the path, and the lettuce will be sown in shorter rows, more often, so that there is never a glut and never a gap.",
        "Body: Whatever is sown, the garden is written up again in the spring, with its pictures, and printed for the shed wall, where last year's sheet has faded but is still legible.",
    ]),

    // The costs' stops, a decimal one with dots, set from the Text tab.
    props: [("Seeds", "tabs", Some("decimal:. 3744000 ."))],
    files: [
        ("The garden in spring.xw", None),
        ("The garden in spring.pdf", None),
        ("Garden notes.md", Some("# Garden notes\n\nSpring 2026. Notes kept as *plain text*, which any editor reads, the **important** parts in bold. More on growing beans at www.example.org whenever it rains.\n\n## To sow\n\n- Beans\n- Peas\n\n## To do\n\n- [x] Dig the bed\n- [ ] Mend the netting\n\n> Sow little and often.\n\nThe rotation, as code:\n\n```\nbeds = [\"roots\", \"legumes\", \"brassicas\"]\nnext = beds[(year + 1) % 3]\n```\n\nYields:\n\n| Crop  | Rows |\n| ----- | ---- |\n| Beans | 2    |\n| Peas  | 3    |\n\nMore peas next year.\n")),
        ("Garden notes.pdf", None),
